adopts `,r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://v3.vitejs.dev/guide/why.html",children:"Vite"}),", a platform-agnostic frontend tool for building web applications. When using the Brightlayer UI ",r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://github.com/etn-ccis/blui-react-cli-templates",children:"React Vite templates"})," to scaffold your new React project it will include ",r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://vitest.dev/guide/why.html",children:"Vitest"}),", the unit testing framework for React Vite projects."]}),`
`,r.jsx(e.p,{children:"Vitest offers compatibility with most of the Jest API and ecosystem libraries and transitioning to Vitest API is highly compatible with Jests API, so existing Jest knowledge can be applied."}),`
`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["If your team prefers Jest, it is possible to use Jest in Vite React setups. ",r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://www.npmjs.com/package/vite-jest",children:"Vite-jest"})," integration for Vite and Jest, so this is a valid option for your unit tests but the preference for Brightlayer UI React Vite applications will be to use Vitest testing framework."]}),`
`,r.jsx(e.h3,{children:"React Templates"}),`
`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["The Brightlayer UI ",r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://github.com/etn-ccis/blui-react-cli-templates",children:"React template"})," projects are pre-configured with ",r.jsx(e.a,{href:"https://v3.vitejs.dev/guide/",children:"Vitest"})," testing framework. When creating a new React Vite project from Brightlayer UI templates, a sample test is created in your project for you (test files are identified by the ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:".spec.tsx"})," or ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:".test.tsx"})," file extension). You can execute the tests by running the following in your terminal:"]}),`
